 Logic Explanation
Light : Reads the LDR sensor from pin A0. If the light level drops below 400 (darkness), digital pin 2 turns ON. Otherwise, it turns OFF.
Fan : Reads the TMP36 sensor from pin A1 and converts the signal to Celsius. If the temperature rises above 30°C, digital pin 3 turns ON. Otherwise, it turns OFF.
Both conditions process concurrently without interrupting each other.


void setup() {
  pinMode(2, OUTPUT);
  pinMode(3, OUTPUT);
}

void loop() {
  if (analogRead(A0) < 400) {
    digitalWrite(2, HIGH);
  } else {
    digitalWrite(2, LOW);
  }

  float celsius = (analogRead(A1) * 0.488) - 50.0;
  if (celsius > 30.0) {
    digitalWrite(3, HIGH);
  } else {
    digitalWrite(3, LOW);
  }
  delay(100);
}
